rt{7}$ and $\\sqrt{7}$ are *not* included. \n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,\\sqrt{7}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n(-\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{7})\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{7}).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting Between Intervals and Inequalities: Open Intervals"}]}
